-*   **Performance:** The adaptive step size control considerably reduces the number of intermediate points used to sample the vector field, allowing strokes to be effectively encoded using only a very small number of line segments [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** High accuracy in field line computation despite tri-linear interpolation; effective culling of back-facing strokes; robust termination prevents artifacts in high-variation regions [S1, unofficial].
