 ## Background
-This method was introduced in the context of interactive volume illustration [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the concept of using curvature fields to guide hatching strokes, ensuring they align with the perceived shape of the volume [S1, unofficial]. The use of RK4(3) with adaptive step size was chosen to balance computational efficiency with visual accuracy [S1, unofficial].
+The method was introduced in the paper "Interactive volume illustration" [S1, unofficial]. It is part of a broader approach to volume illustration that uses hatching strokes to convey shape and structure. The use of RK4(3) integration with adaptive step size control is a key technical contribution to ensure accuracy and efficiency in stroke generation [S1, unofficial].
 
